How Football's Financial Rules Affect Neymar's Resignation to Paris
Provisions restricting the spending of European football clubs do not prevent Neymar's relegation from Spain's Barcelona to Paris Saint-Germain in France.
Of its possible consequences for Paris Saint-Germain (PSG) will be determined by UEFA, which regulates European football, which can prevent teams from attending the prestigious Champions League.
In 2011, UEFA introduced fair-game financial rules, according to PSG to be able to demonstrate that Neymar's transfer has been financed without major losses.
€2,222 million was disbursing Barcelona to end a Brazilian contract, and Neymar's annual salary at the new club is traversing tens of millions of dollars.
