“We will conclude the WADA Road Map in the near future.” – Russian Deputy Prime Minister Vitaly Mutko
Vitaly Mutko, Russian deputy Prime Minister Vitaly Mutko, has said that Russia will soon take to annuities under the World Anti-Doping Agency (WADADA) to reintegrate the powers of RUSADA, the Russian Anti-Doping Agency.
"Some measures have already been put in place under a roadmap, and RUSADA was given the right to design and be tested in cooperation with the British Anti-Doping Agency UKAD.
WADA's roadmap has been upgraded in this regard," Mutko stated on Thursday.
