Mutko says it doesn't involve anything of concern to Russia.
"It's all been announced, and it's all implemented.
The results will be presented to the International Olympic Committee and the WADA in the near future," Mutko added.
However, one of the points on the roadmap presupposes Russian anti-doping authorities to publicly accept the results of an investigation by WADA-appointed Canadian jurist, Richard McLaren. McLaren is investigating the state's alleged role in domining of Russian sport.
Mutko said: "The study is ongoing because our anti-doping system has admitted to a failure.
All measures have been put in place.
We didn't have government programs, we can't admit something that didn't exist.'
