Glint received €10 million from Bessemer Venture Partners in November and has raised a total of 10,000 dollars in funding.
Entrepreneurship is not a surprise in view of the links between companies, corporate culture and venture capital.
According to a number of studies, employees expect more from their jobs.
In competitive markets such as Silicon Valley, good salaries and interesting projects are just the beginning.
Employees want to feel they are accepted and appreciated, giving their time to a genuinely beneficial company.
"Employees make a stronger commitment to a company's success if they thriffee at a company and feel that they're being listened to and that their work is rewarding and rewarding," says Nina McQueen, executive director of Employee Remuneration and Well-Enhancing.
Investors get a return when companies thrive. Companies thrive when employees commit.
