The Birth of a Comics Book: The Story of a Castle
The Little Scotney's Castle in County Kent is now known by Squeeze's music video, as well as Margaret Thatcher's hideout from the 1970s and 1980s.
But it has 700 years of turbulent history. Now, in a charming location in the Bewl River Valley, the subject of a comic book written by Jamie Rhodes, a mastic-haired writer who was fond of old documents.
